# Skipped checks

Exploration Season live mutation was intentionally skipped because it is an accepted non-goal. The six-plugin live plan has no aggregate result file; session-count and serial-dispatch behavior are covered by the focused process-level tests.

# Spec consistency

The implementation, Skill, DD reference, and proposed DD publishing specification agree on one explicit task-scoped native session, official upload wire names, dependency GET/revalidation, WA create defaults, category ID serialization, deterministic failure stages, readback-first uncertainty handling, and credential redaction.

# Known limitations and risks

DD remains dependent on official service projections. A plugin update accepted by the service but absent from both author-list `latest_version` and supplemental detail remains `verification_required=true`; the CLI performs no automatic replay. Real writes require a currently authenticated official client environment and are represented only by the retained, redacted verification records.

# Conclusion

Pass. The requested DD alignment and cross-platform publication workflow are implemented and verified within the declared scope.
